/P 186 0 R
/E (Newman [8] demonstrated that in many actual social networks a person's betweenness centrality can be a more accurate measure of importance than a person's degree centrality \(number of friends\). In character networks, this can indicate a character who sits between two disconnected groups, such as a messenger who is mentioned by both the hero's and the villain's groups, has high betweenness centrality but not necessarily a high mention count. We calculate both metrics so that users can see both perspectives.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
