/E (The recommendations module employs an approach called content based filtering which is implemented by a Ridge regression model. To make recommendations, the user provides a csv file of books they have read with columns title, author, year, publisher, and optionally rating. The user must also provide a large catalogue of un-read books \(Books.csv\).)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
506 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (Features from title, author, year and publisher are calculated with TF-IDF vectorizer. The)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
507 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (model is trained to predict whether the user will like a book they haven't read based on the features and on similarities to the books they have read before. We do 5 fold cross validation to get an estimate of model performance \(AUC, R2 and MAE\). Recommendations are a.\) based on the catalogue books' scores b.\) from 20 top rated books and c.\) with feature level explainability of the prediction.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
